NAME
       init - the first process

SYNOPSIS
       init

DESCRIPTION
       Started by the kernel as pid 1. It mounts the root filesystem,
       restores the saved console font and audio settings, spawns a
       shell on each virtual console and then reaps orphans for the
       rest of the session.

       It is not meant to be run by hand.

FILES
       /etc/vconsole.conf, /etc/audio.conf, /etc/shell

SEE ALSO
       csh(1), setfont(1), mixer(1), shutdown(1)
